00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:22.860
So the reason people crush up aspirin
and use it on their face is because

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:28.410
aspirin is acetylsalicylic acid
salicylic acid is beta hydroxy acid BHA

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:32.520
this is a really common treatment for
clearing out pores, it's a chemical

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:37.500
exfoliant. Acetylsalicylic acid, which is
an aspirin, this has what's called an

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:42.930
acetyl group (surprise) attached to the
hydroxy part of the molecule. It's not

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:47.340
really known whether or not it converts
effectively into salicylic acid on your

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:50.910
skin. It does convert in your digestive
tract. It still probably has

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:54.930
anti-inflammatory properties but it's
not really the same as salicylic acid,

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:58.500
you can't really cheap out and use this
and expect the same results. So I think

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:02.940
using a proper salicylic acid treatment
should work better but this isn't the

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:06.150
worst hack. There is also a slight
concern that if you use an aspirin

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:08.910
tablet and you just mix it with water
you're going to end up with a really

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:12.840
high concentration on your skin. So this
can be quite irritating on your skin

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:17.670
especially because it is still an acid
and so if you have this sort of

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:21.930
irritation it can lead to your pimple
lasting longer, it can lead to

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:26.340
hyperpigmentation, which might take a
while to fade. Again it's just safer to

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:35.190
use a proper salicylic acid product that
is made for applying on the skin.

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:57.659
Glitter near your eyes is usually not a
great idea. Depending on the type of

00:03:57.659 --> 00:04:04.260
glitter, some glitters are made of little
flakes of metal. Metal is sharp, your eyes

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:08.159
are fragile, so if you get a tiny piece
of glitter in your eyes, which is quite

00:04:08.159 --> 00:04:12.090
likely, if you've ever tried using a
really brightly colored eyeshadow you'll

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:16.320
see that it comes out in your tears, so
it is getting into your eye. If it gets

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:21.630
trapped under your eyelid, which again is
not that far-fetched, it can scratch your

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:25.800
cornea and then lead to infections. There
are a few case studies where people have

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:30.360
gotten glitter into their eyes and it
scratched it and it's led to nasty

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:36.270
infections which has led to permanent
damage. Petroleum jelly is not very good

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:41.160
